From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A7om <hatter6822@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] target/arm: Fire a timer whose offset exceeds the count

The virtual timer compares CVAL with the virtual count, the physical
count minus CNTVOFF_EL2 modulo 2^64. When the offset is larger than
the physical count, the virtual count has wrapped to a large value,
and a CVAL a little above it is reached a few ticks later.

gt_recalc_timer() computed the deadline as cval + offset and treated
an overflow of that sum as "never". In this case the sum always
overflows, although the deadline, the sum modulo 2^64, is close, so
the timer never fired: a guest that set CNTVOFF_EL2 above the count
(making the virtual count start below zero) and armed the virtual
timer waited forever.

Compute the deadline as the time left to CVAL, cval - (count - offset)
ticks, added to the count; only that sum overflowing means the
deadline is beyond the 64-bit count. Deadlines that did not involve a
wrapped count are unchanged.
---
 target/arm/helper.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/arm/helper.c b/target/arm/helper.c
index af45234..7755c8f 100644
--- a/target/arm/helper.c
+++ b/target/arm/helper.c
@@ -1530,12 +1530,15 @@ static void gt_recalc_timer(ARMCPU *cpu, int timeridx)
             }
         } else {
             /*
-             * Next transition is when (count - offset) == cval, i.e.
-             * when count == (cval + offset).
+             * Next transition is when (count - offset) == cval, which is
+             * cval - (count - offset) ticks from now: (count - offset)
+             * is below cval, but may itself have wrapped when offset >
+             * count, so count == (cval + offset) only modulo 2^64.
              * If that would overflow, then again we set up the next interrupt
              * for "as far in the future as possible" for the code below.
              */
-            if (uadd64_overflow(gt->cval, offset, &nexttick)) {
+            if (uadd64_overflow(count, gt->cval - (count - offset),
+                                &nexttick)) {
                 nexttick = UINT64_MAX;
             }
         }
